Lets agterm report to agmux's analytics-service (owner.agmux.dev).

- Bodies may carry "app": "agmux" | "agterm" (missing = agmux, so agmux clients are unchanged).
- New POST /v1/events takes a batch of up to 100 events; unknown names and props are dropped.
- agterm events: agent_started {agent}, feature_used {feature}; allow-lists in src/validate.ts.
- installs and daily_active get an app column (migrations/0003_app.sql); /api/summary?app=agterm.

Apply from the agmux repo root:  git apply -p1 <this file>
Then: cd analytics-service && npm run typecheck && npm test
      npx wrangler d1 execute agmux-owner --remote --file=./migrations/0003_app.sql
      npx wrangler deploy
Run the migration before deploying: the new code writes the app column.

